      "label": "Positive Workplace Integration",
      "quote": "Everyone loves a joke. I’m from Guangdong and I’ve got a bit of an accent when I speak Mandarin, so my team leader gave me the nickname Little Canton, and now the whole front office calls me that. It sounds really friendly to me."
    },
    {
      "label": "Cultural Humor and Nicknames",
      "quote": "Sometimes when guests from Hong Kong or Macau phone in, my colleagues shout, Little Canton, it’s for you, and I take the call in Cantonese. The guests are really pleased when they hear it."
    },
    {
      "label": "Language Learning and Sharing",
      "quote": "Last week it was m goi, Cantonese for thank you. Everyone’s pronunciation was really strange, I couldn’t stop laughing, and they laughed too. One colleague wrote m goi on the back of their hand and practised it all day."
    },
    {
      "label": "Colleague Support and Inclusion",
      "quote": "My team leader saw I couldn’t understand, so he got everyone to switch to Mandarin, and he even ordered a Cantonese dish specially, saying it was so Little Canton could have a taste of home."
    },
    {
      "label": "Career Development Opportunities",
      "quote": "There’s a front-desk vacancy next month. My team leader encouraged me to apply. He said being able to speak two dialects is an advantage."
    }
  ],
  "interpretation": "The interviewee describes a supportive and inclusive work environment where colleagues embrace cultural differences through humor, language learning, and shared activities, fostering integration and career growth.",
